I put the tomatoes and spinach in my bag.
Then I look at the other vegetables on the cart.
There is a dark green vegetable there.
That vegetable is very bumpy.
I point at that vegetable.
I ask the vegetable vendor.
"Dada, which vegetable is this?"
He says, "Madam, this is karela."
I ask him, "How does it taste?"
Dada smiles a little.
He tells me, "Madam, it is very bitter."
"Bitter?"
I think.
I do not like bitter food.
I tell Dada, "I do not want karela today."
He nods.
I give him the money for the vegetables.
I take my bag and go ahead.
